'''Bariai''' (also known as '''Kabana''') is an [[Austronesian languages|Austronesian language]] of [[New Britain]].

==Name==
The name {{lang|bch|Bariai}}, literally {{gloss|at the mangrove}}, is derived from {{lang|bch|bare}} {{gloss|[[mangrove]]}} + {{lang|bch|-eai}} {{gloss|locative suffix}}. The alternative name {{lang|aie|Kabana}} comes from the [[Amara language]], meaning {{gloss|foreigner}}.

